WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.299
Hey, Youtube!

00:00:01.299 --> 00:00:05.710
I’m SCP Explained, and this is… also SCP
Explained.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.730
Before we get into today’s story, go ahead
and smash that like button and ring the bell

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:14.150
to be notified every time one of our epic
videos hits your subscription feed.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.580
And don’t forget to share this video with
everyone you know - friends, family members,

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.700
pets, and even that sweaty guy at the bus
stop.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:27.050
Alright, that’s more than enough pandering
to the algorithm for one video… or is it?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:32.390
Because today we’ll be talking about another
one of Dr. Bright’s many misadventures.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.270
For those of you who don’t know - and if
you don’t, I’m wondering why you clicked

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.610
on this video - Dr. Jack Bright is one of
the most chaotic and unpredictable researchers

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.660
working at the Foundation.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.730
His status as an immortal consciousness means
that even his most hair-brained schemes rarely

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.180
have lasting consequences for the man himself.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:57.160
The same cannot be said about the amount of
collateral damage those same schemes cause,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.160
mind you.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.680
And quite recently, Dr. Bright decided to
attempt one of the most dangerous and immoral

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.860
acts that a human being - or humanoid anomaly
- is capable of.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:08.860
That’s right!

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.950
Dr. Bright has started a Youtube channel.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.950
I know.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.630
I should have given a fair warning before
saying something so alarming, but sadly, it

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.810
is true.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.110
And much like every time Dr. Bright gets an
idea like this into his crazy little head,

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:28.430
the rest of us just have to watch and wait
for the inevitable backfire to play itself

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.660
out.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:36.649
So sit back and enjoy the show as Dr. Bright
becomes the aspiring YouTuber, Mr. Bright.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:41.050
The first video on Mr. Bright’s channel
is a short audio-visual remix simply titled

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:42.240
“Clef Music.”

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.479
It begins with Jack Bright sneaking up behind
fellow researcher and occasionally respected

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:51.799
colleague Dr. Alto Clef with a pepperoni pizza
in hand.

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:55.950
Dr. Clef appears to be totally unaware of
Bright’s approach, and is utterly shocked

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:02.070
when Bright smears the entire pizza - cheese,
toppings, sauce, and all across his face.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:06.729
The rest of the video is recording of Clef’s
angered reaction, set to electronic dance

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:11.000
music with certain phrases enhanced through
the use of autotune.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.150
The top comment from user NotKondraki reads
“Oh, I get it!

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.200
His name is Alto Clef, and he’s singing.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.200
XD”

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.300
There’s a reply to that same comment from
user 3ManyGuns that says, “JACK.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.489
DELETE THIS.”

00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:24.710
in all caps.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.550
The video received around one thousand views
over three days, which wasn’t much by the

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.980
standards of most well-known YouTubers, but
it was more than enough encouragement for

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.550
Mr. Bright to keep the content train a-movin.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.060
But what to do next?

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.470
After all, autotune remixes hadn’t been
at the peak of their popularity in almost

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.709
a decade.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:49.629
Prank videos had also evolved to a level of
elaborate absurdity that far surpassed the

00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:52.550
novelty of a pie to the face.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:57.629
Mr. Bright would have to get creative if he
wanted to remain even somewhat relevant in

00:02:57.629 --> 00:03:00.160
the ever-evolving Youtube algorithm.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.970
He eventually decided to release a vlog series
titled “My Life In Site 19”, during which

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:10.280
Bright would film his daily routine in one
of the most secure Foundation containment

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.340
sites in existence.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:17.420
Needless to say, the 05 council had the first
video in the series taken down almost immediately

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.049
via Youtube's copyright strike system.

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:24.300
A breach of classified information like that
couldn’t be allowed to be freely accessed

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.120
on the internet, even if the total views on
the video at the time of the takedown had

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.280
barely cracked three hundred.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:35.430
Jack realized his channel was going nowhere
fast, as only had around ten subscribers,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:40.489
and most of them were members of the research
team that he had personally told to subscribe.

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:44.370
He had to find a way to bring the numbers
up without getting in further trouble with

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.420
the 05 council.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.390
That’s when it hit him!

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:52.680
He’d conceal his identity with some kind
of cartoon avatar - or, as they were sometimes

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.230
known in the YouTube world: a rantsona.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:00.310
Maybe something that sorta looked like him,
but was abstract enough that nobody would

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.480
know there were any ties between his channel
and The Foundation.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.090
So he drew up a few sketches and eventually
settled on a design for his rantsona that

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.870
captured his personality and could be placed
on screen whenever he didn’t want to appear

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.459
on camera.

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:21.340
It was an unfortunate wake-up call when Mr.
Bright found out that not only were caucasian

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:26.750
men with brown hair far from uncommon in the
world of Youtuber rantsonas, a fair amount

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.730
of them also sported glasses.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:33.700
There was at least one other rantsona that
wore a lab coat just like his own.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.430
Before long, Mr. Bright was receiving a ton
of comments comparing him to these other creators,

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:42.040
saying that he was both a rip-off and a trend
chaser.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.050
Mr. Bright couldn’t believe it.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.900
All that work to fit in among the rantsonas,
only to wind up being called generic.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:54.530
But he was nothing if not resourceful, and
the researcher turned Youtuber realized he

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.080
could use this turn of events to his advantage.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.160
He released his next video, titled “Why
I’m Leaving This Community.”

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.860
While he never specified what community he
was leaving, or any specific grievance towards

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:11.910
another Youtuber, Mr. Bright did spend a lot
of time talking about the Youtube terms of

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:17.470
service and how making the like-to-dislike
bar invisible was causing him undue stress

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.520
that had required him to distance himself
from making videos for a while.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.410
He ended the video by firmly stating enough
was enough and that he wouldn’t take it

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:30.100
anymore - again, never specifying what “it”
was.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:34.620
The video got seventeen thousand views in
the first two days since its upload, and the

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:38.620
comments were filled with users applauding
Mr. Bright for his bravery and apparent ability

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.490
to speak his mind.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.260
Overnight his subscribers grew to five hundred,
and countless comments continued to pour in

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:50.300
showing support for the nebulous cause that
Mr. Bright now stood for.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:55.090
Now, this was the response Mr. Bright had
been looking for, and he planned to grow his

00:05:55.090 --> 00:06:00.350
audience even further by playing into the
vague anti-establishment angle that his previous

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.310
video had suggested.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:06.150
He appeared in front of the camera himself
in the video “Youtube Doesn’t Want You

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:11.490
To See This”, this time eschewing all foundation
apparel and filming against a green-screened

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:16.060
background of an absurdly large kitchen with
spotless white cabinets.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:20.560
The kitchen was, of course, a computer-generated
image Mr. Bright had devised to show that

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.220
he was successful and wealthy but also casual
and down to earth.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:29.770
Over the course of the video, Mr. Bright insisted
that some unnamed higher-ups at Youtube were

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:35.520
trying to silence him, and that nearly every
video he made was allegedly being demonetized.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.900
This claim was made, despite the fact that
Mr. Bright was actually not yet able to become

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:44.460
a member of Youtube's partner program because
he hadn’t met the subscriber threshold to

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.280
start earning ad revenue.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:51.690
Still, he was sure that centering himself
in a controversy would be a surefire way to

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.620
gain more subscribers.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.470
However, he was proven very wrong.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:01.470
Within hours of the video's release, the commenters
were tearing Mr. Bright apart, calling him

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.430
a liar and a fake.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.970
Like a pack of tiny amateur detectives, Mr.
Bright’s audience turned on him, and his

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:10.910
reputation began to turn sour.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:15.400
Response videos came out later in the week,
bashing Mr. Bright Youtube channel and accusing

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.960
him - rightfully so - of spreading misinformation.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.840
This was perhaps the biggest setback yet.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.380
Though the channel had grown a bit as he had
hoped, the small fanbase surrounding it had

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.800
turned incredibly defensive.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.740
Every comment section on a video talking about
Mr. Bright was a war zone between self-proclaimed

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.741
Bright stans and anyone unlucky enough to
anger them.

00:07:36.741 --> 00:07:41.880
The worst part was, Mr. Bright himself had
no idea what the arguments were even about

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.120
at this point.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.690
He wasn’t sure what he said or did that
had caused such a polarized reaction.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:52.449
He tried to win the audience back with a few
more Dr. Clef prank videos, but it was no

00:07:52.449 --> 00:07:53.449
use.

00:07:53.449 --> 00:07:58.420
Clef had gotten wise to Bright’s youtube
plans, and whenever he was on screen, he would

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:03.909
speak with so much profanity that the audio
would become basically unusable without being

00:08:03.909 --> 00:08:04.909
censored.

00:08:04.909 --> 00:08:08.129
Additionally, he would fire several of his
guns into the air in a wild and dangerous

00:08:08.129 --> 00:08:09.520
fashion.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:14.060
These factors meant that Jack had to shelve
pretty much every video involving Clef, and

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.099
the ones that he was able to edit all of the
swears and gunshots out of wear borderline

00:08:18.099 --> 00:08:19.099
incomprehensible.

00:08:19.099 --> 00:08:24.479
It was clear enough that the Mr. Bright brand
was on its way out, and Dr. Bright had to

00:08:24.479 --> 00:08:25.800
make peace with that.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.080
He had essentially three options available
to him:

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.810
Rebrand and hope that the previous audience
forgets about the controversy surrounding

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:35.770
the channel.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:41.620
Start an entirely new Youtube channel as if
nothing had ever happened or…

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.060
Give up on being a Youtuber entirely.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.690
Option number 3 certainly wasn’t going to
happen, and to commit to option 2 would mean

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:55.190
losing the subscribers and views he had already
gained, so really only the prospect of a total

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:59.690
rebrand could make any of this seemingly futile
struggle worthwhile.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:01.779
It had to be option one.

00:09:01.779 --> 00:09:05.761
In order for this to work, Dr. Bright had
to choose a new form of content that was so

00:09:05.761 --> 00:09:10.089
low effort that he couldn’t possibly be
perceived as bad at it.

00:09:10.089 --> 00:09:15.230
He had been watching a number of Youtube videos
for research, and eventually, he decided that

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:20.120
reaction content was the ideal way to make
a bunch of videos without having to spend

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.310
too much time on each individual one.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:28.050
All he had to do was wait for other creators
to make the content, and he would record his

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:30.160
unscripted reactions.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.649
He could potentially do this all day, provided
he continued to supply himself with other

00:09:34.649 --> 00:09:36.180
youtube videos.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:41.300
Of course, there was a slight issue of how
he would have to present himself in these

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.330
videos.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:47.820
His face was already somewhat known in the
community at large, and his now all but discarded

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.370
rantsona would cause similar problems.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:54.420
Then, Dr. Bright was struck with another epiphany.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:59.200
During a late-night session of obsessive content
research, which had regretfully been taking

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:04.430
the place of the actual SCP research he was
supposed to be doing, Dr. Bright fell asleep

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.190
on his desk with the autoplay feature on.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:12.950
He awoke several hours later to hear the sounds
of a virtual youtuber - or Vtuber - reacting

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:16.980
to content the same way he was hoping to on
his channel.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.200
A vtuber rig!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.200
Of course!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.089
Dr. Bright thought to himself.

00:10:21.089 --> 00:10:23.230
The answer had been right in front of him!

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:28.000
By rigging his body movements to a 3D animated
character, he would both have a baseline level

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:34.890
of anonymity and the capacity to realistically
translate his reactions into the digital realm.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.520
This was genius!

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:40.690
His channel would soar in popularity once
he created an appealing virtual character

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.380
to embody himself.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:46.570
Goodbye, Mr. Bright, and hello - Vtuber Bright!

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:51.380
But of course, he had to design the avatar
himself, acquire the correct software, and

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:56.750
learn how to utilize all of it before stepping
once again into a world of comparisons to

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.550
similar content.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:03.020
On second thought, this was not going to be
anywhere near as easy as Dr. Bright initially

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.709
thought it would be.

00:11:04.709 --> 00:11:09.089
Perhaps there was no easy to get views on
Youtube, and obtaining positive success and

00:11:09.089 --> 00:11:14.000
notoriety on the platform wasn’t something
that had a simple clear-cut answer.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.020
Maybe this latest venture had taught Dr. Bright
that being himself and focusing on his work

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.200
was…

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.320
Nah, he didn’t learn anything like that.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.930
He just decided to take a big shortcut through
all the real hard work that goes into becoming

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.130
a vtuber.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:32.260
Because when Dr. Bright is faced with a problem
that can’t be overcome through non-anomalous

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:38.350
means, he finds the right SCP for the job
and solves it the supposedly easy way.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.900
With the “supposedly” doing a lot of heavy
lifting in that sentence.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:51.060
In the case of his current vtuber aspirations,
Dr. Bright enlisted the help of SCP-1471 - Ma10.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:55.940
The skull-faced SCP already dwelled inside
of virtual space, and though it was perhaps

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:01.070
just a coincidence based on the specific vtuber
Dr. Bright had stumbled upon: it seemed that

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:06.930
humanoid wolves had been proven to be quite
popular with the typical vtuber audience.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:13.399
Besides, Dr. Bright wasn’t unaware of the,
ahem, sort of people who were always eager

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:20.940
to join SCP-1471’s fan club, er… research
team.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:25.550
With only a few minor modifications to its
programming, Ma10 was able to perform all

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.339
the essential functions of a Vtuber rig.

00:12:28.339 --> 00:12:33.399
Dr. Bright would move his arms or head in
meatspace, and Ma10 would mimic the movement

00:12:33.399 --> 00:12:36.769
like it was some kind of shared game between
the two.

00:12:36.769 --> 00:12:42.720
Since SCP-1471 didn’t have a voice of its
own, Dr. Bright provided a very spirited vocal

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.980
performance through his own microphone.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:50.490
After a few test runs, the dynamic duo of
SCP and researcher had succeeded in becoming

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.810
one complete vtuber.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:57.970
His initial plan to become a popular and well-respected
Youtuber may have failed, and the original

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:02.890
channel name of Mr. Bright soon faded from
the internet’s collective memory, but Dr.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.949
Bright’s determination to keep on grinding
and adapt to new forms of content was something

00:13:07.949 --> 00:13:11.940
that any up-and-coming creator could find
inspiring.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:16.700
That is, unless they too had let countless
hours of important research on dangerous anomalies

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:20.160
fall to the wayside in pursuit of internet
fame.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:24.510
If that is the case, maybe what is best for
some would-be YouTubers not to leave their

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:30.620
day job so soon - especially not when the
lives of millions hang in the balance.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:35.800
Now go check out “SCP-963 What Would You
Do If You Were Immortal Like Dr. Jack Bright?”

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:39.139
and “Can Dr Bright Defeat Billionaire Jeff
Bezos?”

00:13:39.139 --> 00:13:41.380
for more classic Dr. Bright adventures!

